<%# locals: id, messages -- the Turbo Stream replacement target for one
    autosaving field's error slot (cs-studio spec §6.1). The one markup for a
    field's error slot: the `Admin::Columns::*`/`Admin::FieldComponent` slots
    render it on page load (`helpers.render`) and `Admin::AutosaveResponses`
    streams it on every save, so a field looks identical whether its errors
    came from the initial page load or a later autosave replace -- and it is
    always rendered, even with an empty `messages`, since an empty replace is
    exactly what clears a field's stale error once the value that caused it is
    fixed (`Admin::AutosaveResponses#autosave_stream`).

    Design pass spec §4: danger-ink text with a leading "!" so the message
    never relies on colour alone (the glyph is decorative, the message itself
    is what a screen reader reads, tied to its input by `aria-describedby`). %>
<div id="<%= id %>" class="mt-1 text-sm text-danger-ink">
  <% messages.each do |message| %>
    <p class="flex gap-1.5"><span aria-hidden="true" class="font-cs-mono font-semibold">!</span><span><%= message %></span></p>
  <% end %>
</div>
